  "id": "neoteny",
  "term": "neoteny",
  "definition": "Neoteny is the slowing of growth and development, which extends dependence on caring or protective adults and allows juvenile features to continue into later life. In the packet’s developmental context, this prolonged transition makes the move from childhood to sexual maturity more difficult and potentially more stressful.",
